{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Time IV: Parts of the Day",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "For the parts of the day, this is what exists:",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Morning = 朝（ひてぃみてぃ or すどぅみてぃ）",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Noon/Mid-day = 昼（ひる or ふぃる）",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Night = 夜（ゆる）",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Midnight = 夜中（ゆなか）",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Breakfast = 朝物（ひてぃみてぃむん or すどぅみてぃむん）",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Lunch = 朝飯（あさばん）",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dinner = 夕飯（ゆーばん）",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Adding a に to the rest gives you \"at [certain meal] time\".",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Also be careful to avoid thinking 朝飯 as \"breakfast\". That's 朝物. It's like confusing dejeuner and petit dejeuner in French in a sense.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ]
}
